WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.950
Let's explore how Microsoft.Extensions.AI
uses IChatClient and IEmbeddingGenerator
interfaces to abstract AI providers,
enabling flexible integration in .NET
applications.

2
00:00:11.967 --> 00:00:24.117
Keyed dependency injection lets
configuration select AI providers like
Ollama, Azure OpenAI, Azure Foundry, or
ONNX-backed implementations, each with
distinct capabilities and costs.

3
00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:34.183
Here's a concise example showing how to
register multiple IChatClient
implementations with keys and resolve them
via DI, enabling easy swapping by
configuration.

4
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:44.900
Application code depends on the
IChatClient abstraction. Swapping
providers requires no code changes, only
configuration updates, illustrating
provider-neutral design.

